var tafsirData_71 = {
  "1": "\"Indeed, We sent Noah to his people ˹saying to him˺, “Warn your people before a painful punishment comes to them.”\" opens Surah Nuh with a mission after the disgrace of the indulgers on the Day they were warned of. The verse introduces the archetypal Warner before painful punishment.\n\n“Indeed, We sent Noah to his people saying to him, ‘Warn your people before a painful punishment comes to them’” establishes purpose. Sent, or “arsalna,” is the same sending as messengers with clear proofs, Scripture and balance so people may administer justice, and the illiterate messenger reciting, purifying, teaching. Noah’s people are the classic deniers whose stories have reached you pagans, who tasted total loss, whose societies rebelled and were called to severe account. Warning before painful punishment mirrors the keepers asking on each cast “Did a warner not come?” and the Reminder for the whole world.\n\nPainful punishment here is both the floodwater overflowing where We carried you in the Ark and the Fire admitted into after drowning where they found none to help against Allah, and the torment drawing near that makes faces gloomy. Before indicates mercy that warning precedes, as with “We will soon send upon you a weighty revelation” and “Be patient with your Lord’s decree.”\n\nThis follows eyes downcast with disgrace on the warned Day to show that warning was indeed given long before disgrace, as with Nuh’s day and night calling.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat Noah as myth, as ancient fables dismissal does. The Quran presents him as attentive reminder, as the Ark is for attentive ears to grasp.\n\nFor practice, hear Noah’s warning as your warning. The painful punishment bound to come for disbelievers averted by none from the Lord of pathways is still before you. Listen and reason as those in awe without seeing do, protect families, and be among those who pray consistently and give rightful share, so painful punishment is not for you but Gardens held in honour, where you will be told to eat and drink joyfully for days gone by.",
  "2": "\"Noah proclaimed, “O my people! I am truly sent to you with a clear warning:\" records Noah’s opening words after being sent to warn before painful punishment. The address is intimate and clear.\n\n“Noah proclaimed, ‘O my people! I am truly sent to you with a clear warning’” translates “qala ya qawmi inni lakum nadhirun mubin,” O my people, I am to you a clear warner. My people shows kinship, not hostility, as with Moses saying “O my people, why do you hurt me when you know I am Allah’s messenger?” and the Prophet called to his people though they rushed to mock. Truly, or “inni,” and clear, or “mubin,” emphasize that the warning is not vague, as with the Messenger whose duty is only to deliver clearly, the Light in which belief is called, and the Reminder that would humble a mountain.\n\nClear warning here is worship Allah alone, fear Him, and obey me, as next verse details, with forgiveness and delay until appointed time, and with rain, wealth, children, gardens, rivers if they seek forgiveness.\n\nThis follows being sent to warn to show how a warner opens, with peoplehood and clarity.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear clear warning as harshness. Clear is mercy, like the pen’s writing that makes clear, the balance for justice, and the call on Friday to proceed diligently.\n\nFor reflection, receive clear warning as the people of insight take a lesson after expulsion without horse or camel, after garden ashes, after Thamud’s blast and ‘Ad’s wind. Do not press fingers into ears and cover yourselves with clothes as they did, but listen, fear your Lord knowing none should feel secure, and obey the warner, so the painful punishment warned of is averted and the elevated Garden’s near fruit becomes your clear reward.\n\nAdditional note: A clear warning also means the warner’s lineage and character are known, as with the Prophet whose outstanding character and never-ending reward prove he is not insane. Noah’s people knew him as one of their own, as Thamud knew Salih and ‘Ad knew Hud, so denial was not ignorance of the speaker but rejection of the message. Receiving clear warning clearly therefore involves acknowledging the known warner and then worshipping, fearing, and obeying, not pressing fingers into ears and covering clothes.",
  "3": "\"worship Allah ˹alone˺, fear Him, and obey me.\" details the clear warning Noah gave to his people. The three commands are the essential response to the painful punishment before it comes.\n\n“worship Allah alone, fear Him, and obey me” translates “ani ‘budu Allaha wa ittaquhu wa ati‘un,” worship Allah, be mindful of Him, and obey me. Worship Allah alone is the call of every messenger sent with clear proofs, of the illiterate messenger reciting, and of the Lord of easts and wests, the King, Holy, who has no associate-gods to bring. Fear Him is the awe without seeing that has mighty reward, the fear that knows none should feel secure from punishment, that protects families from Fire, and that makes the mindful hear and obey and spend to best ability. Obey me is to follow the warner, as with “whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, whatever he forbids, leave it,” and “obey Allah and obey the Messenger, but if you turn away, Our Messenger’s duty is only to deliver clearly.”\n\nNoah places obedience to himself third, after worship and fear, showing his authority is derivative, not self-glorifying, unlike the despicable brute who is obeyed wrongly.\n\nThis follows clear warning to show content, and precedes “He will forgive your sins and delay your end until appointed time,” showing reward.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to separate these three, as if worship without fear or obedience is sufficient, leading to saying without doing that is despicable.\n\nFor practice, worship Allah alone without idols like Wadd, Suwa‘, Yaghuth, Ya‘uq, Nasr urged by plotters, fear Him as the Most Subtle, All-Aware who knows whether you speak secretly or openly, and obey the warner who calls openly, publicly, privately day and night, so forgiveness and delay until appointed time become yours, and the Gardens where you are held in honour are reached, not the drowning then Fire where none helps against Allah.",
  "4": "\"He will forgive your sins, and delay your end until the appointed time. Indeed, when the time set by Allah comes, it can never be delayed—if only you knew.\" gives Noah’s promise for worship, fear, and obedience. The verse pairs forgiveness with respite, then fixes the limit.\n\n“He will forgive your sins, and delay your end until the appointed time” translates “yaghfir lakum min dhunubikum wa yu’akhkhirkum ila ajalin musamma,” He will forgive you of your sins and delay you to a named term. Forgive sins echoes the sincere repentance that absolves and admits into Gardens under rivers, where light shines ahead and the Righteous will have Gardens of Bliss. Delay until appointed time reflects the way out and provision from sources never imagined for the mindful, and the ease after hardship, but not indefinite postponement of the Inevitable Event that will have come to pass, the appointed Day never delayed, and every soul’s term never delayed when it comes.\n\nIndeed, when the time set by Allah comes, it can never be delayed—if only you knew” stresses that delay is not cancellation, as with “They see it as far, We see it as near,” and “No calamity befalls except by Allah’s Will,” and “Leave them to indulge until they face their Day.” The appointed time, or “ajal musamma,” is written before creation where every calamity or blessing is written, inscribed by the pen, destined for everything. If only you knew indicates they do not grasp seriousness, like those who felt secure that earth will not swallow.\n\nThis follows worship, fear, obey to show incentive, and precedes Noah’s complaint that calls made them run farther, showing promise was rejected.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear forgiveness and delay as bargain to postpone punishment while persisting secretly, as with hypocrites who said we bear witness. Forgiveness requires worship alone, fear, and obeying, not performance like planks leaned worthless.\n\nFor reflection, accept the offer now before the appointed time that cannot be delayed arrives, worshipping alone, fearing rightly, and obeying the warner who calls day and night openly, publicly, privately, so forgiveness is granted and delay is gracious time used to give rightful share, protect families, and walk upright, not to indulge and amuse until the Day you have been warned of.",
  "5": "\"He cried, “My Lord! I have surely called my people day and night,\" reports Noah’s plea after promising forgiveness and delay. The verse shows the warner’s persistence and the people’s response.\n\n“He cried, ‘My Lord! I have surely called my people day and night’” translates Noah’s complaint to his Lord. My Lord indicates trust, as with “in Him we believe and in Him we trust” and the wife of Pharaoh’s “My Lord, build me a house near You.” Day and night indicates continuous calling, as with the Messenger standing for nearly two-thirds of the night reciting, the pen writing, and the reminder to the whole world delivered consistently. Day and night calling mirrors the smoothing of earth for you to move by day and the night worship more impactful, both used for da‘wah.\n\nThis follows forgiveness and delay offer to show that despite offer, the call was extended persistently, not once, similar to Moses calling his people and being hurt, and to the illiterate messenger reciting, purifying, teaching among those previously clearly astray.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear day and night calling as harassment. It is mercy that warns before painful punishment, as with keepers asking “Did a warner not come?” to establish that warning did come.\n\nFor reflection, the warner’s day and night calling invites day and night listening. Those who listened and reasoned would not be among Blaze residents who lament if only we had listened, but among those in Gardens held in honour. When the call comes, whether at night more impactful or at Friday when you are to proceed diligently, answer rather than run farther away as next verse says they did, so the appointed time that can never be delayed finds you among the submitted, not the wicked.\n\nExtra reflection: Day and night calling also shows that guidance does not keep office hours. The Reminder recited properly in a measured way at night and the remembrance of the Name wholeheartedly by day both carry the same call. Noah’s day and night persistence models the Messenger who stands nearly two-thirds of the night and the believers who remember often after dispersing to seek bounty. To answer day and night calling, be present both in night impact and day occupation, so the appointed time that never delays finds you among those who listened in both seasons.",
  "6": "\"but my calls only made them run farther away.\" describes the effect of Noah’s day and night calling. The people’s response was increased flight.\n\n“but my calls only made them run farther away” translates “fa-lam yazidhum du‘a’i illa firara,” my call did not increase them except in flight. Firar is to flee, run, escape, as with spooked zebras fleeing from a lion from the reminder, and as with hypocrites who thought every cry against them and were lost in delusion. Running farther away shows that the warning that should have drawn them to forgiveness and delay until appointed time instead drove them deeper into persisting in disobeying and following elites who devised tremendous plot and urged not to abandon idols.\n\nThis follows day and night calling to show that persistence of the warner was met with persistence in aversion, as with those who persist in arrogance and aversion when provided for, and those who were called to prostrate when fully capable but chose not to.\n\nThe increase, or “lam yazid,” indicates that every additional call, openly, publicly, privately, only added to distance, like the garden owners’ whisper to exclude poor that proceeded early fixated, and like the disbelievers who rush headlong toward the Prophet to mock.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to blame the caller for the flight, as if clear warning repels. The flight is due to sealed hearts after believing then abandoning, to hearts that became hard after long time, to the despicable traits of withholder, transgressor, evildoer.\n\nFor the living, the warning is to not let calls make you run. When you are invited to be forgiven by pressing not fingers into ears, to seek forgiveness for He is Most Forgiving and will shower abundant rain, wealth, children, gardens, rivers, and when you are told to worship, fear, obey, stay, do not run. Instead, be among the excepted who hear and obey and are properly observant, so the caller’s day and night effort is not your flight but your return, and the appointed time finds you delayed graciously, not seized with crushing grip.",
  "7": "\"And whenever I invite them to be forgiven by You, they press their fingers into their ears, cover themselves with their clothes, persist ˹in denial˺, and act very arrogantly.\" details the physical rejection that caused running farther away. The verse gives four acts.\n\n“And whenever I invite them to be forgiven by You, they press their fingers into their ears, cover themselves with their clothes, persist in denial, and act very arrogantly” translates Noah’s description of his people’s response to the invitation “seek your Lord’s forgiveness, for He is Most Forgiving.” Fingers into ears is to block hearing, the opposite of attentive ears that grasp the Ark reminder and of “if only we had listened and reasoned.” Covering with clothes is to hide the face from the warner, similar to the worthless planks that impress but hide, and to turning heads in disgust when told to come for forgiveness.\n\n“persist in denial” translates “asarrū,” they insisted, as with societies that rebelled and were called to severe account, and “act very arrogantly” translates “wa-stakbaru istikbaran,” they magnified arrogance, as with the garden owners’ fixated purpose and the brute’s arrogance because blessed with wealth and children. The pair shows insistence plus height, the same arrogance that made faces gloomy when torment drew near.\n\nThis follows running farther to show how running looks, and precedes “Then I called them openly, publicly, privately,” showing Noah varied methods despite rejection.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see this as cultural quirk. It is universal, as with those who leave business on Friday for merchandise, who rush headlong to mock, and who say ancient fables when revelations are recited.\n\nFor reflection, do not press fingers into ears when invited to be forgiven, nor cover yourself with clothes to avoid the warner. Instead, uncover, listen, reason, and walk upright, so the invitation to forgiveness becomes the forgiveness that writes Gardens held in honour, not the persistence that writes the raging Flame that summons hoarders and rips scalps.",
  "8": "\"Then I certainly called them openly,\" continues Noah’s account after describing fingers pressed and clothes covered. The verse shows his variation in method.\n\n“Then I certainly called them openly” translates “thumma inni da‘awtuhum jiharan,” then I called them aloud, openly, manifestly. Openly contrasts with pressing fingers to block; it is the public call that the Messenger also does as his duty is only to deliver clearly, as with the call on Friday to proceed diligently and the pen that writes what everyone writes openly. Noah’s open call mirrors the Messenger’s recitation to bring from darkness to light, the balance so people may administer justice, and the Reminder that would humble a mountain, all delivered openly.\n\nThis follows the physical rejection to show that Noah did not retreat after they persisted in denial and acted arrogantly, but persisted himself, beautifully patient as commanded, not like Jonah in distress. It also precedes “then I preached to them publicly and privately,” showing escalation from open to public and private.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think open calling excuses private neglect. Noah did both, as the warner must, so no excuse remains that the call was hidden.\n\nFor the listener, open calling invites open listening. When the warner calls openly with “worship Allah, fear Him, obey me,” and promises forgiveness and delay until appointed time, respond openly, not by running. Be among those who hear and obey to best ability, who give rightful share to the asker and deprived, and who are properly observant, so open calling finds you open, and the painful punishment warned of before it comes is averted, and the elevated Garden with near fruit becomes your open, joyful welcome.\n\nFurther, openly calling ensures that even those who cover themselves with clothes and press fingers into ears cannot claim they did not hear. Open call is public proof, like the two witnesses bearing true testimony for Allah in divorce, the pen writing openly, and the balance so people may administer justice. It is the opposite of Satan-inspired secret talks that grieve, and of the garden owners’ whisper to exclude poor. Openly is therefore mercy that leaves an open record, so the Day presentation where no secret stays hidden has an open invitation already recorded, and the painful punishment warned of cannot be said to have come without warning.",
  "9": "\"then I surely preached to them publicly and privately,\" completes Noah’s method after openly calling. The verse shows comprehensive approach.\n\n“then I surely preached to them publicly and privately” translates “thumma inni a‘lantu lahum wa asrartu lahum israra,” then I announced to them and I confided to them secretly. Publicly, or “a‘lantu,” is to declare, as with the noble Messenger’s recitation to the whole world and the Friday call; privately, or “asrartu,” is to whisper individually, as with good private talk for goodness and righteousness that does not grieve, not like Satan-inspired secret talks. Noah used both, covering the spectrum from openly to secretly, day and night, as with the Messenger standing for nearly two-thirds of the night and reciting properly in a measured way.\n\nThis follows openly to show that no avenue was left untried, similar to the garden sensible one urging “Did I not urge you to say Allah willing?” and the helpers’ love that preferred emigrants publicly and privately despite need.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see public and private preaching as intrusive. It is mercy that warns before painful punishment, as with the keepers’ question “Did a warner not come?” that establishes warning came in all forms.\n\nFor reflection, hear both. When the Reminder is recited publicly on Friday, proceed diligently; when privately you are invited to be forgiven, do not press fingers into ears. Let public and private calls make you among the submitted not wicked, whose record will be read happily, whose life is bliss in elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, not among the arrogant who persist and act very arrogantly and whose faces will be gloomy when torment draws near.\n\nMore: Publicly and privately also respects that some hearts are reached in public awe and others in private counsel. The sensible one who urged “say Allah willing” spoke privately to the group, while Noah’s public call addressed the crowd. Both are needed because wealth and children divert both publicly through fanfare and privately through household pressure to withhold. Hearing both ensures that whether you are the asker or the deprived, the rightful share, the sincere repentance that perfects light, and the elevated Garden become accessible. Let both calls make you submitted, so your record happily says “Read my record.”",
  "10": "\"saying, ‘Seek your Lord’s forgiveness, ˹for˺ He is truly Most Forgiving.\" records Noah’s first counsel when he preached publicly and privately. The invitation is to seek forgiveness as the entry to all that follows.\n\n“Seek your Lord’s forgiveness, for He is truly Most Forgiving” translates “istaghfiru rabbakum innahu kana ghaffara,” seek pardon from your Lord, He has been ever Forgiving. Most Forgiving, or “Ghaffar,” is intensive, indicating repeated, abundant forgiveness, as with All-Forgiving, Most Merciful who forgives the mindful and the repentant. Noah invites them to be forgiven by You, not by idols Wadd, Suwa‘, Yaghuth, Ya‘uq, Nasr that elites urged not to abandon. Seeking forgiveness is the opposite of pressing fingers into ears and covering with clothes, persisting and acting arrogantly. It is the opening that makes abundant rain, wealth, children, gardens, rivers possible, as next verses detail.\n\nThis follows “I preached publicly and privately” to show content. Noah did not preach himself, but forgiveness, as with the Reminder that would humble a mountain and the Ark carried as reminder.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think seeking forgiveness is mere words. Seeking includes turning, as with sincere repentance that absolves and admits into Gardens, where light shines and is perfected.\n\nFor practice, seek forgiveness now as Noah urged. The appointed time that can never be delayed is still ahead, so seeking today can still bring rain, provision, and Gardens. Seek with the garden owners’ “Glory be to our Lord, we have been wrongdoers,” and with “My Lord, forgive me, my parents, and whoever enters my house in faith,” so the Most Forgiving who showered rain and supplied gardens responds and the painful punishment warned of is averted.\n\nFurther, Most Forgiving, or “Ghaffar,” invites repeated seeking, not a single utterance. Noah’s people needed to seek forgiveness that would also make them abandon idols Wadd and Nasr, whose tremendous plot urged not to abandon, and turn from leading many astray. Seeking forgiveness that is Most Forgiving therefore involves leaving the plot, not just saying words, similar to sincere repentance where you turn to Allah, He absolves and admits into Gardens, light shines, and He is Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing who multiplies the good loan.",
  "11": "\"He will shower you with abundant rain,\" promises the first earthly result of seeking forgiveness. The gift is immediate and tangible.\n\n“He will shower you with abundant rain” translates “yursil al-sama’ ‘alaykum midrara,” He will send heaven upon you pouring abundantly. Midrara is copious, continuous rain, like the rain that delights planters then becomes chaff, but here as mercy, not delusion. Abundant rain was vital in an agrarian society where harvests that could be reduced to chaff while you lament “we have been deprived” depended on rain that could be made salty. Shower indicates generosity, not a drizzle.\n\nThis follows seeking forgiveness to show that forgiveness brings not only pardon in the Hereafter where Gardens of Bliss await, but also provision in this world, as with “We will soon send upon you a weighty revelation” and “provide for them from sources they could never imagine.” It mirrors the later promise to supply wealth, children, gardens, rivers, showing a sequence where heaven’s water precedes earth’s wealth.\n\nThe promise also counters the elite’s plot that wealth comes through idols. Rain comes from the Lord of pathways, the Most Capable who holds all authority, who descends command between seven heavens, who adorned the lowest heaven with lamps, and who holds birds aloft. Idols like Wadd and Nasr have no rain.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat rain as automatic proof of piety, leading to boasting that honour will expel inferior. Rain is a test of best deeds, as with garden test as We tested Meccans, and as with wealth and children are only a test.\n\nFor daily life, seek forgiveness and expect rain, but use it gratefully. Let abundant rain remind you to give rightful share to beggar and poor, to let the poor enter your garden today, and to say “Allah willing,” so rain does not become the flood that overflowed where We carried you in the Ark, but the abundant rain that feeds gardens and rivers you enjoy with thanks, walking upright on the smoothed earth that He spread for you.",
  "12": "\"supply you with wealth and children, and give you gardens as well as rivers.\" continues the worldly promises for seeking forgiveness, adding wealth, progeny, orchards, and flowing water.\n\n“supply you with wealth and children, and give you gardens as well as rivers” translates “wa yumdidkum bi-amwalin wa banin wa yaj‘al lakum jannatin wa yaj‘al lakum anhara,” He will extend you with wealth and children and make for you gardens and rivers. Supply, or “yumdidkum,” is to extend, increase, as with treasuries of heavens and earth belonging to Allah and honour belonging to Allah, not to the despicable withholder who said ancient fables because blessed with wealth and children. Wealth and children here are the same wealth and children that were warned not to divert from remembrance and that are only a test, but now as gifts in response to seeking forgiveness, they become blessed rather than diverting.\n\nGardens and rivers echo the Gardens of Bliss with the Lord for the righteous, the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach and you are told to eat and drink joyfully, and the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever promised to those who believe and do good. Giving gardens and rivers in this world is a foretaste, as with abundant fruit never out of season nor forbidden for the people of the right, and the better garden hoped for after turning.\n\nThis follows abundant rain to show that rain leads to gardens and rivers, wealth and children follow, all from seeking forgiveness, not from idols.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think forgiveness is a transaction to get wealth, turning worship into merchandise fanfare that drew crowds from the pulpit. Forgiveness is sought for its own sake, with wealth as additional mercy, as with provision from sources never imagined and ease after hardship for the mindful.\n\nFor practice, seek forgiveness with the sincere repentance that perfects light, and receive wealth, children, gardens, rivers as trusts to be shared. Let wealth provide according to means for waiting women, let children be raised to guard chastity and testify devoutly like Mary, let gardens’ rightful share go to the deprived, so wealth and children become the great reward with Allah, not the true losers’ diversion.",
  "13": "\"What is the matter with you that you are not in awe of the Majesty of Allah,\" questions the people after listing forgiveness and worldly gifts, exposing lack of reverence.\n\n“What is the matter with you that you are not in awe of the Majesty of Allah” translates “ma lakum la tarjuna lillahi waqaran,” what is with you that you do not hope for, expect, revere Allah’s grandeur. Waqar is majesty, dignity, gravity, the same majesty that makes seven heavens one above another without flaw where you look again and find no flaw, that adorns lamps as missiles, that smooths earth for you, and that will make earth swallow as it quakes and stones unleash if you feel secure.\n\nNot being in awe mirrors the garden owners’ fixated purpose without “Allah willing,” the brute’s ancient fables because blessed with wealth, the deniers’ rush to mock, and the challenging question “What is the matter with you? How do you judge?” about equating submitted and wicked.\n\nThis follows gardens and rivers to show that gifts should inspire awe, not delusion that a powerless force will help.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear awe as fearful paralysis. Awe here is hope for majesty, reverent expectation that leads to worship, fear, and obedience as Noah first said, and to listening and reasoning so you are not among residents of Blaze.\n\nFor reflection, be in awe of Majesty by looking at how He created you in stages, how He created seven heavens, moon as reflected light, sun as radiant lamp, how He caused you to grow like a plant and spread earth for pathways. That awe replaces wealth and children as diverters with wealth and children as supplied gifts, and replaces persistence in disobeying with seeking forgiveness, so majesty is not the raging Flame that rips scalps but the elevated Garden where you are held in honour.",
  "14": "\"when He truly created you in stages ˹of development˺?\" supports the call to awe of Majesty by pointing to your own creation. The argument is personal and observable.\n\n“when He truly created you in stages of development” translates “wa qad khalaqakum atwara,” He has created you in stages, phases. Stages include sperm-drop emitted, clinging clot, developing and perfecting form producing both sexes, growing from earth like a plant, and being dispersed over earth, all referenced in “Do people think they will be left without purpose? Were they not once a sperm-drop, then a clot, then He developed and perfected?” and “He shaped you perfecting form.” Stages are visible in wombs, in infants, in growth, proving the One who smooths earth and adorns lamps is the same who fashions you.\n\nThis follows “What is the matter that you are not in awe?” to give reason to be in awe. The One who stages your creation can shower rain, supply gardens, and carry you in the Ark, and can bring you forth again after returning you to earth.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think stages deny divine act, as if stages mean nature self-creates, similar to thinking withholder of good self-provides. Stages are the manner of the All-Wise Creator, the Most Subtle, All-Aware who knows whether you speak secretly or openly, the Knower of seen and unseen who shaped you.\n\nFor practice, remember stages when you see wealth and children, gardens and rivers, and when you are tempted to abandon idols for Wadd etc. Stages show you are dependent, not self-made, so awe of Majesty should lead to seeking forgiveness, worshipping alone, fearing, and obeying, so the stages that led from drop to plant-like growth end not in drowning then Fire where none helps, but in elevation to Gardens held in honour where attentive ears grasp.",
  "15": "\"Do you not see how Allah created seven heavens, one above the other,\" invites cosmic observation after personal stages, expanding awe from self to heavens.\n\n“Do you not see how Allah created seven heavens, one above the other” translates “alam tara kayfa khalaqa Allahu sab‘a samawatin tibaqa,” have you not considered how Allah created seven heavens in layers? Seven heavens one above another echoes the same verse in Surah al-Mulk, “You will never see any imperfection in the creation of the Most Compassionate. So look again: do you see any flaws? Then look again, sight returns frustrated and weary,” and “We adorned the lowest heaven with lamps.” It also recalls the command descends between them so you may know He is Most Capable and encompasses all knowledge, and the seven heavens and likewise for earth.\n\nOne above another, or “tibaqa,” indicates layered perfection, without support you perceive, flawless, adorned, and protected as missiles against eavesdropping devils.\n\nThis follows stages to show that the same Creator who stages you layers heavens, both requiring awe of Majesty.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat seven heavens as mythic. The Quran presents them as real, Created by the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority, Most Capable of everything.\n\nFor reflection, do see how He created seven heavens. Look again and again, see no flaw, see lamps, then see moon and sun within them next, see earth spread for pathways, and let seeing become awe, so you are not among those who asked “When will this threat come?” or who feel secure that One in heaven will not swallow, but among those in awe without seeing whose mighty reward is forgiveness, who walk upright, not crawl facedown, whose gathering is not with everyone on earth to ransom but with light ahead.\n\nExtra: One above the other, or “tibaqa,” also recalls the command descending between seven heavens so you may know He is Most Capable and encompasses all knowledge. The One who layers heavens can also layer your stages of development from drop to plant-like growth to walking pathways, all without flaw in purpose, even if you do not see flaw when you look again. That layering should move you from not being in awe of Majesty to being in awe, so you are not among those who persist in disobeying and following wealth that increases only in loss, but among those whose provision is from sources never imagined.",
  "16": "\"placing the moon within them as a ˹reflected˺ light, and the sun as a ˹radiant˺ lamp?\" details two lights within the seven heavens just mentioned. The verse distinguishes their natures.\n\n“placing the moon within them as a reflected light, and the sun as a radiant lamp” translates “wa ja‘ala al-qamara fihinna nura wa ja‘ala al-shamsa siraja,” made the moon a light, or “nur,” reflected, and the sun a lamp, or “siraj,” blazing. Reflected light versus radiant lamp captures the moon’s borrowed glow and the sun’s self-radiant heat, a distinction modern observation confirms but the Quran stated without instruments. The moon within them indicates it is within the heavens’ system, and the sun as lamp indicates its intense, lamp-like brilliance that, like the adorned lamps as missiles, serves adorning and marking.\n\nThis follows seven heavens to show two adornments that are also timekeepers and guides, as with points of sunrise and sunset whose Lord is truly capable to replace, and the merging of night into day.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to worship the moon or sun, as those who did not abandon idols like Yaghuth, Ya‘uq, and Nasr did with celestial idols. They are created lights, not deities, as “He is Allah, there is no god except Him” and “He is the Lord of east and west, there is no god worthy except Him” declare.\n\nFor daily awe, see the moon’s soft reflected light and sun’s radiant lamp as signs of majesty, as with hearing, sight, intellect hardly thanked, and let them guide you to seek forgiveness, so He showers abundant rain and makes gardens and rivers, and to walk upright, so the Day the moon is dimmed and sun and moon are brought together does not catch you among the wicked who wish to ransom with everyone on earth, but among the bright faces looking at their Lord.",
  "17": "\"Allah ˹alone˺ caused you to grow from the earth like a plant.\" traces human origin to earth, linking heavens, moon, sun to your growth.\n\n“Allah alone caused you to grow from the earth like a plant” translates “wa Allahu anbatakum min al-ard nabata,” Allah germinated you from the earth as a growth. Anbata is to sprout, as with seed sown “is it you who cause it to grow or is it We?” and with growing from earth like a plant in stages. The earth is the same smoothed for you to move and spread for spacious pathways, the same to which He will return you and bring you forth again, and the same from which the garden owners’ garden was struck.\n\nLike a plant emphasizes dependency, gradual growth, and need for rain that He showers for the forgiven, gardens and rivers, and for the Most Compassionate who holds birds and smooths earth.\n\nThis follows moon and sun to show that just as He placed lights in seven heavens, He grew you from earth, both acts of the same Majestic whose awe you lack.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think growing like a plant denies human dignity. The plant simile is for origin and growth, not for worth; you are given hearing, sight, intellect, honour belonging to Allah, and the Pen’s writing, so you are more than plant, but your beginning is plant-like to humble those who say ancient fables because blessed with wealth.\n\nFor reflection, remember you were grown like a plant, so do not persist in disobeying like those who followed elites with tremendous plot urging not to abandon idols. Seek forgiveness, be in awe, and let your growth end not in drowning then Fire with no helper, but in being brought forth again to Gardens held in honour where sincere repentance perfects light.",
  "18": "\"Then He will return you to it, and then simply bring you forth ˹again˺.\" continues the plant cycle after growing from earth. The verse states return and re-emergence.\n\n“Then He will return you to it, and then simply bring you forth again” translates “thumma yu‘idukum fiha wa yukhrijukum ikhraja,” then He will return you into it and bring you forth with a bringing. Return to it is burial, the earth and mountains crushed with one blow, you presented with no secrets hidden, the earth that was smoothed for you now receiving you. Bring you forth again is resurrection, as with reassembling bones and fingertips, the Day they come forth from graves swiftly as if racing to an idol, the Trumpet’s one blast, and the Inevitable Event that will have come to pass.\n\nThen simply, or “ikhraja,” emphasizes ease, as this is easy for Allah who created seven heavens without flaw, caused you to grow, and spread earth for pathways.\n\nThis follows growing like a plant to show the full cycle, sowing, return, and harvest, mirroring the garden owners’ harvest and the chaff that delighted then withered.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to doubt bringing forth, as disbelievers claimed “we will not be resurrected. Yes, by your Lord you will surely be resurrected and that is easy.” Growing and returning prove bringing forth is consistent.\n\nFor practice, live as one who will be returned and brought forth. Move about the spacious pathways to seek bounty and remember often, protect families, give rightful share, and walk upright, so returning is to earth as a believer and bringing forth is to an elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, not to the raging Flame that summons those who gathered and hoarded.\n\nAdditional: Returning to earth and bringing forth again also mirrors the Ark where you were carried when floodwater overflowed, a reminder for attentive ears, and the Trumpet’s one blast where earth and mountains are lifted and crushed and the Inevitable has come to pass. The same Most Capable who spread earth for spacious pathways can return you to it as a seed and bring you forth as a plant, as with abundant rain that He showers after forgiveness. So returning is not dread for the forgiven, but the path to being brought forth to Gardens held in honour, where fruit hangs within reach and you are told to eat and drink joyfully.",
  "19": "\"And Allah ˹alone˺ spread out the earth for you\" reiterates the smoothed earth after detailing growing, returning, and bringing forth. The earth is presented as spread.\n\n“And Allah alone spread out the earth for you” translates “wa Allahu ja‘ala lakum al-arda bisata,” Allah made earth a carpet, expanse. Bisata is a wide mat, as with “He smoothed out the earth for you, so move about in its regions and eat from His provisions. And to Him is the resurrection,” and “We spread out the earth for you to walk along its spacious pathways.” Spread indicates stability for walking, building, and pathways, not swallowing as it quakes violently for those who feel secure, and not unleashing stones for those who deny.\n\nAlone emphasizes that no idol like Wadd or Nasr spread it, and no powerless force will help instead of the Most Compassionate.\n\nThis follows bring forth again to show that the same earth that receives and returns also serves in the interim as spread, for movement and provision, before resurrection.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think spread means flat earth denial of creation’s shape. Spread is about usability, spacious pathways, not about denying the layers of seven heavens or points of sunrise and sunset whose Lord is capable.\n\nFor daily awe, see spread earth as majesty to revere, walk along spacious pathways to seek forgiveness, gardens, rivers, and to call openly and privately as Noah did, so spreading is not for indulgence and amusement until you face your Day, but for taking the Right Way to your Lord, where attentive ears grasp and the reminder benefits.\n\nMore: Spread out as “bisata” also invites you to see the earth’s expanse as trust, not as honour that expels inferior or as merchandise better than what is with Allah. Spread is for walking with purpose, like the Messenger reciting to bring from darkness and the disciples standing with Jesus. It is the opposite of the raging Flame that rips scalps and summons hoarders who gathered and hoarded wealth. Using spread rightly is to walk its spacious pathways to call openly and privately as Noah did, day and night, so spreading becomes your way to forgiveness and Gardens and rivers, not to drowning then Fire where none helps.",
  "20": "\"to walk along its spacious pathways.’”\" explains why earth was spread. The purpose is movement.\n\n“to walk along its spacious pathways” translates “li-tasluku minha subulan fijaja,” to go through its pathways, broad valleys. Pathways, or “subul,” are routes, as with Lord of pathways of heavenly ascent where angels ascend on a Day fifty thousand years, and with spacious pathways He spread for you. Fijaj are wide, open passes between mountains, showing earth is not a maze of swallowing quakes but an open network for travel, trade, and da‘wah, as Noah walked to warn and the Messenger spread the Reminder to the whole world.\n\nSpacious indicates ease, opposite to the dunes of shifting sand on the Day earth and mountains shake violently and mountains become dunes, and to the chain of seventy arms that restricts.\n\nThis follows spread out earth to show that spreading’s purpose is to walk, not to feel secure that One in heaven will not cause swallowing, as earlier warned, but to move with remembrance.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to use spacious pathways solely for indulgence and amusement until they face their Day, or for hoarding and withholding, or for rushing headlong to mock from right and left.\n\nFor practice, walk spacious pathways for the purposes Noah did, calling to worship, fear, and obedience, seeking forgiveness so He showers rain and supplies wealth, children, gardens, rivers, and walking for the Reminder that perfects light, so your walking along pathways in this world prepares you for being brought forth again and walking upright on the Straight Path, not crawling facedown, toward Gardens held in honour where even more spacious pathways await.\n\nExtra: Spacious pathways, or “subulan fijaja,” wide valleys, also recall the pathways of heavenly ascent where angels and the spirit ascend on a Day fifty thousand years, whose Lord is truly capable to replace mockers with better. Earthly spaciousness is a gift to prevent feeling secure that He will not cause swallowing as it quakes or stones to unleash, because spaciousness is provided, not earned by strongholds. Walking them to seek forgiveness and gardens, rather than to devise tremendous plots urging idols, turns spacious into spacious provision, where He supplies wealth, children, and rivers as He promised the forgiven.",
  "21": "\"˹Eventually,˺ Noah cried, “My Lord! They have certainly persisted in disobeying me, and followed ˹instead˺ those ˹elite˺ whose wealth and children only increase them in loss.”\" reports Noah’s complaint after his public and private preaching and the people’s pressing fingers, covering clothes, persisting, acting arrogantly. The verse shifts from invitation to grievance.\n\n“Eventually, Noah cried, ‘My Lord! They have certainly persisted in disobeying me, and followed instead those elite whose wealth and children only increase them in loss’” translates his observation. Persisted in disobeying, or “‘asawni,” they opposed, disobeyed, as with each disobeying their Lord’s messenger, so He seized them with crushing grip. They followed instead those elite, or “ittaba‘u man lam yazidhu maluhu wa waladuhu illa khasara,” they followed one whose wealth and children increased him only in loss, as with the brute with abundant wealth and children who says ancient fables, the despicable withholder whose wealth did not help, and the garden owners whose wealth diverted. The elite’s tremendous plot urged not to abandon idols, leading many astray.\n\nIncrease them in loss, or “khasara,” mirrors true losers who let wealth or children divert from remembrance and residents of Blaze who lament, and total loss tasted by societies that rebelled.\n\nThis follows walking pathways to show that pathways can be misused to follow the elite instead of the warner.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to blame wealth and children per se. Wealth and children increase in loss only when they are used to persist in disobeying, to devise plots, and to urge idols.\n\nFor reflection, do not follow those whose wealth and children increase them in loss, but follow the warner who says “Seek forgiveness, He is Most Forgiving,” so your wealth and children become supplied gardens and rivers, not loss, and your pathways walk leads to being forgiven by the All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.",
  "22": "\"and who have devised a tremendous plot,\" adds detail to the elite Noah complained about, after stating they are followed despite wealth and children increasing them in loss. The plot is the strategy to maintain idolatry.\n\n“and who have devised a tremendous plot” translates “wa makaru makran kubbara,” they plotted a great plot, immense cunning, like the despicable’s slander and gossip-mongering, the hypocrites’ false oaths as shields, and the garden owners’ whisper to exclude poor. Tremendous plot included urging not to abandon idols, especially the five named, and leading many astray, as with “Those elite have already led many astray. So O Lord, only allow wrongdoers to stray farther.” The plot’s greatness is in its scope, involving generations, as with societies that rebelled and were called to severe account.\n\nThis follows persisted in disobeying and following elite, showing how following was secured through plot, not argument.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think plot means clever politics not applicable today. Tremendous plots today include making wealth merely circulate among rich, making oaths binding until the Day whatever you decide, and calling revelations ancient fables.\n\nFor the living, recognize the plot and do not follow it. Follow the warner who calls openly, publicly, privately, day and night, who says worship, fear, obey, so He will forgive and delay until appointed time, and provide gardens and rivers. That following saves from being among those drowned then admitted into Fire with none to help against Allah, and places you among those who enter houses in faith with Noah’s prayer for forgiveness.\n\nFurther: Tremendous plot, or “kubbara,” also includes whispering “Do not let any poor enter your garden today” and “Do not spend on those with the Messenger,” both withholding good that makes true losers. The plot’s greatness is measured by how many it leads astray, as with “那些 elite have already led many astray.” Recognizing plot as plot, not wisdom, is what the Most Subtle, All-Aware who knows whether you speak secretly or openly enables. Exposing it allows you to choose the warner’s public and private preaching over the elite’s secret urging, so you are not among the drowned with none to help but among the forgiven who enter houses in faith.",
  "23": "\"urging ˹their followers˺, ‘Do not abandon your idols— especially Wadd, Suwâ’, Yaghûth, Ya’ûq, and Nasr.’\" quotes the elite’s tremendous plot, naming the idols. The verse preserves history and warns against idol persistence.\n\n“urging their followers, ‘Do not abandon your idols— especially Wadd, Suwa‘, Yaghuth, Ya‘uq, and Nasr’” lists five idols from Noah’s people, understood as righteous men later idolized, whose names persisted among Arabs at the Prophet’s time, showing continuity of the plot. Wadd, Suwā‘, Yaghūth, Ya‘ūq, Nasr were worshipped as intercessors, like later associate-gods they were asked to bring forth if truthful, and like the honour claimed to expel inferior, and like merchandise fanfare that diverted from Friday remembrance.\n\nThis follows devised tremendous plot to show content, and precedes those elite have already led many astray.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit idols to named statues. Idols include whatever is taken alongside Allah, wealth that diverts, children competed in, and honour that expels.\n\nFor practice, abandon idols as Noah urged. Worship Allah alone, fear Him, obey the warner, seek forgiveness, and be in awe of Majesty who created you in stages, seven heavens, moon, sun, earth plant-like, and spread pathways, so you are not among those who persist and are drowned then admitted into Fire, but among those forgiven, delayed until appointed time, supplied with gardens and rivers, and eventually among believing men and women forgiven with Noah.\n\nAdditional: The five idols are also a lesson in how righteous men become idols when memory is idolized. Wadd, Suwa‘, Yaghuth, Ya‘uq, Nasr were, in tradition, pious predecessors whose statues were first memorials then objects, showing how tremendous plot uses sentiment. The same happens when wealth and children, gardens and rivers are taken as idols that supply without the Most Forgiving. Not abandoning idols therefore means abandoning whatever you follow instead of those elite whose wealth increase loss, and instead following the warner who says worship, fear, obey, so you are not among the wicked who will say “We have certainly been transgressors” after turning on each other, but among those who trust for a better garden.",
  "24": "\"Those ˹elite˺ have already led many astray. So ˹O Lord˺, only allow the wrongdoers to stray farther away.”\" is Noah’s observation and supplication after quoting their idol urging. The verse links leading astray to a prayer for increased straying as recompense.\n\n“Those elite have already led many astray. So O Lord, only allow the wrongdoers to stray farther away” translates “wa qad adallu kathiran wa la tazidi al-zalimin illa dalala,” they have led many astray, and increase the wrongdoers only in straying. Led many astray, or “adallu kathiran,” is the same leading astray as with the despicable who hinder from the Way, the slanderer and gossip-monger who divide, and the withholder who makes wealth circulate only among rich. Many indicates generations, as with the garden test, ‘Ad’s wind, and Pharaoh’s grip, all after being led by elites whose wealth increased them in loss.\n\nOnly allow the wrongdoers to stray farther away, or “la tazidi al-zalimin illa dalala,” is Noah’s prayer that persistence not be rewarded with guidance, but that straying deepens, as with “So when they persistently deviated, Allah caused their hearts to deviate, for Allah does not guide the rebellious” and “This is because they believed then abandoned, so hearts were sealed, so they do not comprehend.” Wrongdoers, or “zalimin,” are those who place loyalty wrongly, following idols instead of worshipping alone, as with submitted vs wicked inequality.\n\nThis follows idol urging to show consequence, and precedes drowning then Fire, where they found none to help, showing prayer answered.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think Noah’s prayer is vindictive. It is justice after day and night, open, public, private calling and pressing fingers, covering clothes, persisting, arrogance, tremendous plot, and leading many astray, all rejected.\n\nFor reflection, do not be led astray by elites, follow the warner’s worship, fear, obey, so you are not among wrongdoers whose straying only increases, but among those who seek forgiveness and are showered with rain, wealth, gardens, and whose house in faith is prayed for.",
  "25": "\"So because of their sins, they were drowned, then admitted into the Fire. And they found none to help them against Allah\" states the recompense for their sins after Noah’s prayer to increase wandering for wrongdoers.\n\n“So because of their sins, they were drowned, then admitted into the Fire. And they found none to help them against Allah” translates “mimma khati’atihim ughriqu fa-udkhilu naran fa-lam yajidu lahum min duni Allah ansara,” due to their sins they were drowned then entered into Fire, and they found no helpers besides Allah. Sins, or “khati’atihim,” include pressing fingers, covering, persisting, arrogance, tremendous plot, urging idols, leading many astray, as with societies that rebelled and tasted horrible punishment, with Garden owners reduced to ashes, and with hypocrites whose severe punishment is prepared.\n\nDrowned then admitted into Fire shows two punishments, drowning in floodwater that overflowed where We carried you in the Ark, and then Fire immediately after, as with being seized with crushing grip and then admitted. Then, or “fa,” indicates sequence without delay, as with the Inevitable Event that will have come to pass with one blast and one crushing.\n\nAnd they found none to help them against Allah, or “ansara,” helpers, as with “which powerless force will help instead of the Most Compassionate? They are lost in delusion,” “No defender can avert punishment for disbelievers from the Lord of pathways,” and “neither wealth nor children will help against Allah whatsoever.” Idols Wadd, Suwa‘ etc. did not help.\n\nThis follows straying prayer to show answer, and precedes Noah’s prayer to leave no disbeliever.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see drowning as merely ancient flood without moral lesson. It is reminder for attentive ears to grasp, as with the Ark.\n\nFor practice, avoid sins that lead to drowning then Fire, worship alone, fear, obey, seek forgiveness so He showers rain rather than flood, supplies gardens rather than drowning, and carries you as He carried you in the Ark to Gardens held in honour, where none of your secrets stay hidden but you are told to eat joyfully.",
  "26": "\"Noah had prayed, “My Lord! Do not leave a single disbeliever on earth.”\" records Noah’s supplication after the drowned then Fire account. The prayer is for total cleansing after total rejection.\n\n“Noah had prayed, ‘My Lord! Do not leave a single disbeliever on earth’” translates “wa qala Nuhun rabbi la tadhar ‘ala al-ardi min al-kafirina dayyara,” leave not on earth a remaining disbeliever. Dayyara is one who remains, inhabits. The prayer follows “because of their sins they were drowned” and before “if You spare any, they will mislead Your servants and give birth only to wicked sinners,” showing Noah’s reasoning that remaining would continue leading many astray and devising tremendous plot, not abandoning idols.\n\nThe prayer’s context is after centuries of day and night, open, public, private calling, pressing fingers, covering clothes, persisting, arrogance, and after his observation that they followed elites whose wealth increase loss and whose plot was tremendous. It is not hasty anger like Jonah’s departure in distress, but a prophet’s judgment after long patience, similar to the command to be patient with the Lord’s decree but also to leave rejecters to Allah.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to apply this prayer universally to wish destruction on all disbelievers in every era. It is specific to Noah’s people whose hearts were sealed after believing then abandoning, persisting, and whose sins led to drowning, and whose remaining would only mislead, as next verse explains.\n\nFor reflection, the prayer shows that warning has an end. The appointed time that can never be delayed when it comes will indeed come, and painful punishment before it will come after warning. To avoid being among “do not leave a single” prayed against, be among “My Lord, forgive me, my parents, whoever enters my house in faith, and all believing men and women,” so you are among the carried in the Ark, the attentive ears that grasp, and the elevated Garden’s residents, not among the drowned with none to help.",
  "27": "\"For if You spare ˹any of˺ them, they will certainly mislead Your servants, and give birth only to ˹wicked˺ sinners, staunch disbelievers.”\" gives Noah’s reason for praying to leave no disbeliever.\n\n“For if You spare any of them, they will certainly mislead Your servants, and give birth only to wicked sinners, staunch disbelievers” translates “innaka in tadharhum yudillu ‘ibadaka wa la yalidu illa fajiran kaffara,” if You leave them they will lead Your servants astray and will beget only a debauched, ungrateful disbeliever. Mislead servants echoes “Those elite have already led many astray,” the withholder, slanderer, transgressor pattern, and the despicable who hinders from the Way.\n\nGive birth only to wicked sinners, staunch disbelievers, or “fajiran kaffara,” extremely debauched, intensely disbelieving, shows that remaining would perpetuate sin across generations, as wealth and children only increased them in loss and as they urged not to abandon idols for descendants.\n\nThis follows not leaving a single to show that eradication was to cut misguidance’s reproduction, similar to the command to protect families from Fire whose fuel is people and stones.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think Noah declares children predetermined. It is observation that their nurturing would produce only such, as they would raise children on idolatry, like elite’s tremendous plot.\n\nFor practice, ensure your own parenting does not give birth to wicked, staunch disbelief, but raises those who guarded chastity like Mary, prayed like Pharaoh’s wife, and are submissive, faithful, devout, repentant, as with better wives hoped for. Seek forgiveness that showers rain, wealth, children as blessed, not as increase in loss, so your children are among Gardens and rivers, not among fajiran kaffara.\n\nMore: “Fajiran kaffara,” or wicked sinner, staunch disbeliever, also describes the despicable profile not to be obeyed: vain oath-taker, slanderer, gossip-monger, withholder, transgressor, brute, whose wealth says ancient fables. Their children, raised on that profile, would repeat it, as the elite led many astray already. Noah’s observation is not about genetics but about nurturing in that plot-filled environment. To avoid giving birth to such, raise children as Noah prayed—forgive me, parents, whoever enters my house in faith, and all believing men and women—in faith, guarding chastity, being true to trusts, and walking upright, so children become the gardens and rivers supplied after forgiveness, not the loss-increasing wealth.",
  "28": "\"My Lord! Forgive me, my parents, and whoever enters my house in faith, and ˹all˺ believing men and women. And increase the wrongdoers only in loss.”\" closes Surah Nuh with a prayer that balances mercy for the faithful and loss for persisters.\n\n“My Lord! Forgive me, my parents, and whoever enters my house in faith, and all believing men and women. And increase the wrongdoers only in loss” translates Noah’s final supplication. Forgive me covers the warner himself, who though outstanding, still seeks forgiveness, as with the Messenger told to seek forgiveness for wives’ faltering and the believers told to turn in sincere repentance so light is perfected. My parents includes lineage, as with Ibrahim’s exception for his father before clarity, now Noah includes parents in faith. Whoever enters my house in faith is specific hospitality, the Ark as house and later the house of faith, echoing “whoever enters my house in faith” and the helpers who loved emigrants, and the later principle to make room. All believing men and women is universal, as with later supplicants “forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith and do not allow bitterness,” and the Garden’s excellent provision for those who believe and do good.\n\nAnd increase the wrongdoers only in loss, or “wa la tazidi al-zalimin illa tabara,” increase not but in ruin, is the counterpart, similar to “only allow wrongdoers to stray farther.” Loss, or “tabara,” is destruction, as with the garden reduced to ashes, societies tasting total loss, and the Fire’s raging Flame.\n\nThis follows not leaving a single and the reason about misleading and begetting only fajiran kaffara, showing Noah’s prayer covers both mercy and justice.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear “increase wrongdoers only in loss” as personal vindictiveness. It is divine justice after day and night, open, public, private calling and pressing fingers, covering, persisting, arrogance.\n\nFor daily practice, pray this prayer. Seek forgiveness for self, parents, household guests in faith, and all believing men and women, and accept that persistence in withholding good, calling ancient fables, and feeling secure against swallowing will only increase in loss, so choose forgiveness now before the appointed time that can never be delayed arrives, and be among the carried in the floating Ark who become attentive ears grasping the reminder."
};